<item>
            <title>[LU-20794] &apos;lfs find --printf&apos; inconsistent directive semantics for symlinks pointing at directories</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20794</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;There are two classes of incorrectness here, depending on whether the symlink-dir was reached as a path passed directly via the cli or via recursive exploration. As this changes the metadata retrieval paths.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When the symlink-dir path is directly passed via the CLI, ordinary stat metadata directives will show the value for the dir inode itself, not the link. This is inconsistent with how symlink-files are handled, where the value of the link inode is always used.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When a symlink-dir path is reached via recursion, layout directives %L{c,i,o,S} use the directory&apos;s child-file default layout if the dir has a default LOV layout, when they should use values from the dir inode itself, matching symlink-file handling.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
